Redeploying a folder now replaces the existing site in place instead of failing with `ErrHostnameInUse`:

- `internal/command/deploy.go:117` — `siteToReplace` lets a folder deploy take over an existing *static* site at the same host; image deploys and folder-vs-app collisions still conflict.
- `internal/command/deploy.go:91` — `redeploy` reuses the app's name, host, TLS, keys, env, resources (flags still apply), swaps `Source`, and relies on `Application.Deploy` for the zero-downtime container/proxy swap. A failed redeploy leaves the old version serving and never destroys the app.
- Tests: `TestSiteToReplace`, `TestRedeploySettings` in `internal/command/deploy_test.go`; `TestStaticSiteRedeploy` in `integration/docker_test.go`.

Verification: `make test` passes, `make lint` (golangci-lint) reports 0 issues, and `TestStaticSiteRedeploy` passes against Docker.
